\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Per-expert normalized trust \(\bar  \alpha _k\) (mean \(\pm \) std over seeds on the modal branch; \(200\) seeds total; \(n{=}500\), \(q{=}0\)) under the shared head; experts are labeled reliable (R), noisy (N), or adversarial (A). Under a reliable majority, Stabilized recovers high reliable trust with near-zero noisy / negative adversarial trust (3R1N: \(\bar  \alpha _R\approx 0.88\), \(\bar  \alpha _N\approx 0\); 3R1A: \(\bar  \alpha _R\approx 0.84\), \(\bar  \alpha _A\approx -0.84\)). Standard on 3R1N/3R1A more often lands on the flipped branch (Table~\ref {tab:synthetic-branch}). Under 1R3A, Stabilized locks onto the flipped branch.}}{10}{figure.caption.13}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:synthetic-branch}{{2}{10}{Per-expert normalized trust \(\bar \alpha _k\) (mean \(\pm \) std over seeds on the modal branch; \(200\) seeds total; \(n{=}500\), \(q{=}0\)) under the shared head; experts are labeled reliable (R), noisy (N), or adversarial (A). Under a reliable majority, Stabilized recovers high reliable trust with near-zero noisy / negative adversarial trust (3R1N: \(\bar \alpha _R\approx 0.88\), \(\bar \alpha _N\approx 0\); 3R1A: \(\bar \alpha _R\approx 0.84\), \(\bar \alpha _A\approx -0.84\)). Standard on 3R1N/3R1A more often lands on the flipped branch (Table~\ref {tab:synthetic-branch}). Under 1R3A, Stabilized locks onto the flipped branch}{figure.caption.13}{}}
