\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Expert-ratio sweep over every mixture of \(n_A\) adversarial and \(n_N\) noisy experts (remainder reliable; \(K{=}10\); shared head; \(n{=}500\), \(q{=}0\); \(100\) seeds per cell; cell values annotated). Rows: \textbf  {(a)}~correct-branch rate; (b) to~(d)~mean learned trust \(\bar  \alpha _A\), \(\bar  \alpha _N\), and \(\bar  \alpha _R\) (all seeds; not conditioned on branch; white when that type is absent). Columns: \textbf  {(i)}~Standard, \textbf  {(ii)}~Stabilized. The dashed line marks \(\#\text  {reliable}=\#\text  {adversarial}\). Stabilized shows a sharp transition at the dashed line. Standard is sticky: weak under reliable majority, nearer chance under adversary majority.}}{14}{figure.caption.20}\protected@file@percent }
